From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kv-cache <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vllm: gate LMCacheMPConnector's load path on num_external_tokens

Backport of the guard from vLLM #47505 / LMCache #4028, which pairs with
vLLM #46865. #46865 is ALREADY PRESENT in this image and is what arms the bug
this fixes -- the two must ship together, and right now only the first half is
here.

Before #46865, MultiConnector.update_state_after_alloc() handed empty blocks to
every non-chosen sub-connector. #46865 changed it to hand them the request's
REAL blocks with num_external_tokens=0, because an offload connector needs
blocks on every request or it can never populate a cold prefix. The new contract
is therefore: gate LOADING on num_external_tokens, NOT on whether blocks is
empty. Most connectors already did; LMCacheMPConnector does not.

lmcache_mp_connector.update_state_after_alloc() never reads num_external_tokens
at all -- it appears only in the signature and the docstring. The state machine
decides purely on tracker.needs_retrieve(), which compares
num_lmcache_hit_blocks > num_vllm_hit_blocks and knows nothing about whether
this connector won the lookup. So when LMCache holds a prefix but NixlConnector
was the chosen connector, the non-chosen LMCacheMPConnector now sees real blocks
and wrongly moves PREFETCHING -> WAITING_FOR_LOAD, creating retrieve tasks for a
load that must not happen.

The leak is the worse half. In that same branch, `condition` also selects how
much of the lookup lock range is released: false frees ALL locked chunks
(num_lmcache_hit_blocks), true frees only the vLLM-computed prefix
(num_vllm_hit_blocks) on the assumption that the retrieve will release the rest.
For a non-chosen connector no retrieve ever runs, so the remainder is never
freed, and end_session() does not release lookup locks either. The locks
accumulate for as long as the server runs.

Gating `condition` on num_external_tokens fixes both halves at once, which is
why this is a one-line change rather than two. num_external_tokens == 0 sends
the tracker straight to READY *and* selects the free-ALL branch, which is
precisely the "transition directly to READY and release lookup locks" the
upstream fix describes. Block tracking above the hunk is deliberately left
unconditional -- that is the store path, and starving it is the bug #46865
exists to fix.

Fires only under MultiConnector[NixlConnector, LMCacheMPConnector] -- i.e.
exactly the MP disaggregated-prefill topology, and not on either P/D pair this
branch currently runs, which are in-process LMCacheConnectorV1.

DO NOT VERIFY THIS WITH A NEEDLE TEST. The unguarded build returns correct
answers and full needle counts; the symptom is spurious retrieve tasks and
lookup locks that never drop, so it degrades under sustained load rather than
failing a short run. Verify by mechanism: no PREFETCHING -> WAITING_FOR_LOAD
transition on a non-chosen connector, and lock count returning to baseline
across a run.

THIS PATCH ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH -- it must ship with patches/0011.

An earlier revision of this header claimed the vLLM copy is the one that loads,
reasoning from KVConnectorFactory registering "LMCacheMPConnector" against this
module. That is true but incomplete, and the conclusion drawn from it was wrong.
At the bottom of this same module, _resolve_lmcache_mp_connector() hands off:

    if os.environ.get("LMCACHE_USE_UPSTREAM_MP"):  -> the class in THIS file
    try: from lmcache.integration.vllm.lmcache_mp_connector import ...
                                                   -> that file  (default)
    except ImportError:                            -> the class in THIS file

LMCache is installed, so on a stock deployment the DEFAULT resolves to
lmcache/integration/vllm/lmcache_mp_connector.py and this patch is a no-op --
it applies cleanly, the build succeeds, and the bug survives untouched. 0011
patches that copy. This one still matters: it covers LMCACHE_USE_UPSTREAM_MP=1
and the ImportError fallback, both of which reach the class defined here.

The error was caught by running the mechanism check against an UNPATCHED image
and watching it fail inside the *other* file. Registration is not resolution --
check where execution actually lands before deciding which copy to patch.

Upstream LMCache #4028 is still open and #47294 was closed as the wrong fix
direction, so re-check both before dropping this patch.

Carried out-of-tree. See README.md.
---
--- a/vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/lmcache_mp_connector.py
+++ b/vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/lmcache_mp_connector.py
@@ -836,7 +836,11 @@
             tracker.append_block_ids(new_block_ids)
 
         # Update the state of the tracker
-        condition = tracker.needs_retrieve()
+        # Gate the LOAD path on num_external_tokens, not on `blocks`: since
+        # vLLM #46865 a non-chosen MultiConnector sub-connector receives the
+        # request's real blocks and must not load. 0 also frees ALL lookup
+        # locks below, which is what stops them leaking.
+        condition = num_external_tokens > 0 and tracker.needs_retrieve()
         if tracker.state == LMCacheMPRequestState.PREFETCHING:
             # If need to retrieve, change to WAITING_FOR_LOAD
             # Otherwise, change to READY
